      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9, we need to find the least common multiple (LCM) of these numbers. The LCM of a set of numbers is the smallest number that is divisible by all of them.\n\nTo find the LCM, we can use the prime factorization method:\n\n1. Find the prime factorization of each number from 1 to 9:\n   - 1: 1 (no prime factors)\n   - 2: 2\n   - 3: 3\n   - 4: 2^2\n   - 5: 5\n   - 6: 2 * 3\n   - 7: 7\n   - 8: 2^3\n   - 9: 3^2\n\n2. Identify the highest power of each prime number that appears in the factorization of any of the numbers:\n   - 2^3 (from 8)\n   - 3^2 (from 9)\n   - 5 (from 5)\n   - 7 (from 7)\n\n3. Multiply these highest powers together to get the LCM:\n   LCM = 2^3 * 3^2 * 5 * 7 = 8 * 9 * 5 * 7 = 2520\n\nTherefore, the smallest number divisible by integers 1 through 9 is \\boxed{2520}.",
